 get it going  that's first the second thing I'd also  tell you is it'll teach you about the  types of clients you're going to get  it'll teach you about location they'll  teach you about how to write a bill  this we can learn from whoever you're  working with whatever company you're  working out of and it'll more  importantly bring in money that we'll be  able to fund your expansion so if you're  able to start this business off out of a  different location and you're making  some money you know now you have some  money to invest back into the business  your and up to the point where you can  go and get your own location now you're  investing from profits and you're not  pulling out of your your own pockets or  going out and getting a loan and  invested for it I'm putting you know  yourself on the line financially you  know potentially for a very long time  for so that's what I do to start  honestly go find another business in a  related field and find some way to  partner up with them where you're doing  your car wash service out of their  location it's not ideal I know you know  you wanna you have the big vision and  that's awesome but you want to take baby  steps every day and make sure you're  doing something every day to take that  business and make it go forward you'll  figure out if you want to do this  business or not you'll be investing back  into the business from profits and it's  honestly one of the best ways you can go  and build your business a great example  just to tell you is my wife's company is  a salsa business and she started by  working at a gym so she teaches people  how to dance if she'll teach 6,000  people here in Toronto how to dance  salsa and it's easy to go up and and  spend money on this right you can go and  buy a look an office or rent an office  and and drop tens and tens or hundreds  of thousands of dollars on this location  and how nice it is but who knows what is  going to work or not who knows if you  even like this business or 